==============================================================================
  ||s||           = 4.312344e+00    D70 4.312344e+00
  s'y_QoI         = +7.313133e-01   D70 +7.313133e-01   <- MEASUREMENT
  s'y_penalty     = +3.719261e-04   D70 +3.719261e-04   <- IDENTITY 2*lam*||s||^2, never gated on
  R_qoi = s'y/||s||^2 = +3.932573e-02   D70 +3.932573e-02
  rho (Gaussian prior metric, 2*lam_L2) = 1.9663e+03   D70 1.966e+03
  lognormal prior metric at beta == 1 (prior mode)         : s'H_prior s = +3.025061e-04   rho_LN = +2.4175e+03
  lognormal prior metric at the reinversion eval-10 field  : s'H_prior s = +5.370458e-03   rho_LN = +1.3617e+02
  lognormal prior metric at the reinversion final field    : s'H_prior s = +1.186466e-02   rho_LN = +6.1638e+01

  A Rayleigh quotient LOWER-BOUNDS the top generalised eigenvalue, so a correct
  rank-6 posterior on this problem returns lambda_1 at or above the numbers
  above. They span 6.2e+01 to 2.4e+03 -- a 40x spread, driven entirely by the
  223 cells pinned at beta = 0.2, where the lognormal prior curvature
  2*lam*(1-log b)/b^2 is 65x its value at b = 1. THAT SPREAD IS WHY THE
  REPLACEMENT DOES NOT BAR ON THIS NUMBER DIRECTLY: a bar at 2.4e+03 would be
  a bar on which state the MAP lands in. It is used as the independent
  EXPECTATION behind a bar of 10, declared in R4.

  NEGATIVE CONTROL (mismatched pair, no shared state):
    s(reinv)'y(inv)/||s_reinv||^2 = +1.2887e-04  against the matched +3.9326e-02
    s(inv)'y(reinv)/||s_inv||^2   = +1.7640e-02  against the matched +1.2172e-04

  NULL N3 sign-randomised y_QoI, 200 draws: mean -7.4891e-03 sd 1.1226e-01  ->  measured is 6.6 sd from the null

