R4  THE REPLACEMENT GATE, EVALUATED -- and the negative controls firing
==============================================================================
  stand-in rank-6 posterior: total prior variance 11812.5, variance removed 3.2757 = 0.0277% of it; largest per-cell sd reduction 0.0143%
  THAT is what rank 6 in 21,000 dimensions looks like, and section 5 says so.

  BAR_A lambda_1 >= 10
  BAR_B  s'Hs in [2.4377e-01, 2.1939e+00]  around the archived 7.313133e-01
  BAR_C  0 < total variance removed <= s^2 * sum_i lam_i/(1+lam_i), the rank bound

  treatment                                                  OLD   NEW A/B/C   lambda_1     s'Hs        var removed/entitled
  W  prior reported as posterior                            PASS  FAIL  F/F/F   0.000e+00  +3.719e-04  0 / 0
  M  plateau beta paired with the eval-1 gradient           FAIL  FAIL  F/F/F   0.000e+00  +3.719e-04  0 / 0
  Z  spectrum taken from the prior alone (eigenvalues == 1)  PASS  FAIL  F/F/F   1.000e+00  +3.719e-04  5906 / 1.688
  H  correct spectrum, Hessian-vector product in the wrong frame  PASS  FAIL  P/F/P   2.418e+03  +2.397e-03  3.276 / 3.276
  Q  real spectrum, credible intervals asserted not derived  PASS  FAIL  P/P/F   2.418e+03  +7.313e-01  1.181e+04 / 3.276
  R  a genuine rank-6 low-rank Laplace posterior (stand-in)  PASS  PASS  P/P/P   2.418e+03  +1.024e+00  3.276 / 3.276

  READ THIS AS THE 2x2 IT IS. The OLD gate cannot tell W, Z, Q or R apart:
  it returns PASS for all four, because none of its three legs is a function
  of any covariance, credible interval or Hessian. The NEW gate returns PASS
  for R alone. W fails all three: no curvature computed, so leg A gets 0, leg B
  gets the prior identity 2*lam*||s||^2 back, and leg C sees no interval move.
  Z fails all three too, and differently: it read its spectrum off the prior,
  so lambda_1 is identically 1 and its intervals remove 5,906 units of variance
  against an entitlement of 1.69. H fails leg B alone, which is the point of B --
  the science is right and the instrument is in the wrong frame; Q fails leg C
  alone: it removes 11,808 units of variance where a rank-6 posterior with its
  own reported spectrum is entitled to remove 3.37, a factor of 3,500.

  M is the mismatched-evaluation error that produced the 1.684 confusion. It
  is the one treatment the OLD legs DO catch, which is why they are retained
  under their own name as G-P4a, the gradient reproduction control, rather
  than deleted. G-P4a FAILS M at ratio 0.501974 against 0.998441.

==============================================================================
R5  IDENTITY TEST APPLIED TO THE REPLACEMENT ITSELF (the two W-2 questions)
==============================================================================
  Q1  WHAT RESULT WOULD MAKE THIS GATE FAIL?
      Leg A: lambda_1 < 10 at the lognormal MAP, i.e. the data does not beat
        the prior by 10x in even its single best direction. Reachable: it is
        the neighbourhood of falsifier F2, and it is what an ill-posed inverse
        problem with a 21,000-dimensional parameter and 6 informed directions
        may genuinely look like once the prior is widened from sigma 0.043.
      Leg B: the first Hessian-vector product returning s'Hs outside
        [2.438e-01, 2.194e+00]. Reachable: the finite-difference
        step, the sign convention, and the design-variable ordering are each
        capable of moving it, and R3's cross-pair control moves it by two
        orders of magnitude, far outside the band.
      Leg C: intervals that do not move, or that remove more variance in
        total than the reported rank and spectrum entitle them to. Both
        exhibited above, by W and Z on the lower side and by Q on the upper.

  Q2  COULD A WRONG TREATMENT STILL PASS?
      YES, and the holes are named rather than papered over.
      (i) A treatment whose lambda_1 is right and whose EIGENVECTORS are
          wrong passes all three legs. Leg C bounds the magnitude of the
          interval tightening, not its location. Closing that needs a second
          external referent on a direction, which this stage does not have.
      (ii) A treatment that reports the archived secant value back instead of
          computing an Hv passes leg B. Mitigation, pre-registered: the run
          must ALSO report the raw Hv vector, its norm, the finite-difference
          step used, and the symmetry check v1'Hv2 against v2'Hv1 that section
          5 already requires, with v2 drawn from numpy default_rng(20260814),
          a direction whose curvature is on no disk in this lab.
      (iii) The MAP arm itself is not graded by this gate at all. G-P1, G-P2
          and F3 grade it. This gate grades the posterior only, which is what
          the strategy PROOF clause asks for and what G-P4 never did.

  Q3  IS ANY LEG DERIVABLE BY CONSTRUCTION FROM ITS OWN INPUTS?  (rule W-2)
      Leg A: no. lambda_1 needs Hessian-vector products, which need adjoint
        solves. No closed form in (beta, lambda) supplies one.
      Leg B: no, in BOTH directions. The reference value s'y_QoI needs
        grad_eval010 from a run this item does not perform; the reported
        value needs an adjoint solve this item does perform. Two independent
        computations of the same scalar.
      Leg C: PARTIALLY, and it is scored accordingly. The entitlement ceiling
        s^2*sum_i lam_i/(1+lam_i) IS derivable from the spectrum, so the UPPER side of
        leg C is a consistency check on the treatment's own arithmetic and
        adds no information about nature. The LOWER side is not derivable and
        is what fails W. Stated here so nobody later reads leg C as evidence.
      The quantity in this whole analysis that IS a pure identity --
        s'y_penalty = 2*lam_L2*||s||^2, printed in R3 -- is reported and is
        gated on nowhere, which is what rule W-2 prescribes.
